Subject: [PATCH] The adoption reverted the _auto_leg stub fix too, and the
 suite went red again

Same adoption, same class as the organ it deleted: the two 1-arg `_auto_leg` stubs were restored
to their pre-fix form against HEAD's 2-arg `_auto_leg(e, n)`, so
`test_auto_legs_under_department_plans_run_only_in_rest` failed with "takes 1 positional argument
but 2 were given" the moment the suite ran again. Re-applied in both test files.

Also records what the guard's backfill recovered on its first cold start with the new lookback:
the full pass history folds correctly, including the two consecutive REACHED_EPILOGUE passes
(pre-warm 1288 s / 81,588 failed, then 1591 s / 88,246 failed) that the 2 MB window had been
silently stepping over.

